# Words codespell would otherwise flag, one per line, lowercase.
#
# couldn: from couldn&rsquo;t in the HTML — codespell sees the word split at
# the entity and reads the half. The prose is correct as written.
couldn

# labelledby: part of aria-labelledby, whose spelling is fixed by the ARIA
# spec and is not a dialect choice. An American-English pass turned it into
# aria-labeledby across four dialogs, which is not an attribute at all, so
# every one of them lost its accessible name and nothing noticed.
labelledby

# tye: the ID3v2.2 frame that holds the year, spelled TYE in the spec. The
# three-character names are all abbreviations and several read as typos.
tye
